---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="SDA Compass"
  scrollBar
  description="SDA Compass scores a swimmer's academics, athletics, and activities, then measures each score against the students a specific school actually enrolls. One report, school by school."
  extraDisclaimer="School examples are illustrative and do not refer to specific institutions. Descriptions of other services reflect the methodology those services publish themselves. The description of our own methodology is simplified for clarity and does not disclose our proprietary scoring formulas, weights, or thresholds."
>

<!-- ==========================================================
     HERO — what the Compass is, in three sentences
     ========================================================== -->
<header class="hero">
  <div class="hero-bg"><div class="glow"></div><div class="grid"></div></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="compass-wrap fx">
        <svg class="compass-hero" viewBox="0 0 340 340" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A compass with three bearings, Academics, Athletics and Activities, around a Fit center">
          <g transform="translate(10,10)">
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="122" fill="#0A1E38" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="2"/>
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="112" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="6" stroke-dasharray="1.3 6.6" opacity="0.5"/>
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="98" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.35"/>
            <g stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round">
              <line x1="160" y1="62" x2="160" y2="40"/>
              <line x1="244.9" y1="209" x2="263.9" y2="220"/>
              <line x1="75.1" y1="209" x2="56.1" y2="220"/>
            </g>
            <g fill="#C9A13B" opacity="0.38">
              <polygon points="160,160 203.3,135 158,156.5"/>
              <polygon points="160,160 203.3,135 162,163.5"/>
              <polygon points="160,160 160,210 156,160"/>
              <polygon points="160,160 160,210 164,160"/>
              <polygon points="160,160 116.7,135 158,163.5"/>
              <polygon points="160,160 116.7,135 162,156.5"/>
            </g>
            <polygon points="160,160 172,134 160,70" fill="#2C5688"/>
            <polygon points="160,160 148,134 160,70" fill="#D9B968"/>
            <polygon points="160,160 176.5,183.4 237.9,205" fill="#2C5688"/>
            <polygon points="160,160 188.5,162.6 237.9,205" fill="#D9B968"/>
            <polygon points="160,160 143.5,183.4 82.1,205" fill="#2C5688"/>
            <polygon points="160,160 131.5,162.6 82.1,205" fill="#D9B968"/>
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="22" fill="#16395E" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="160" y="165" text-anchor="middle" fill="#D9B968" font-family="Fraunces, serif" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1">Fit</text>
          </g>
          <g>
            <polygon points="160,12 170,7.5 180,12 170,16.5" fill="#D9B968"/>
            <path d="M180 12 L180 18" stroke="#D9B968" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <text x="170" y="34" text-anchor="middle" fill="#FFFFFF" font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="13.5" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="1.5">ACADEMICS</text>
            <g stroke="#D9B968" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round">
              <path d="M277 250 q4 -3.5 8 0 q4 3.5 8 0"/>
              <path d="M277 255 q4 -3.5 8 0 q4 3.5 8 0"/>
            </g>
            <text x="285" y="281" text-anchor="middle" fill="#FFFFFF" font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="13.5" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="1.5">ATHLETICS</text>
            <path d="M55 242 L58.2 249 L65 252 L58.2 255 L55 262 L51.8 255 L45 252 L51.8 249 Z" fill="#D9B968"/>
            <text x="55" y="281" text-anchor="middle" fill="#FFFFFF" font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="13.5" font-weight="500" letter-spacing="1.5">ACTIVITIES</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <span class="eyebrow fx d2"><span class="dot"></span> SDA Compass</span>
      <h1 class="fx d3">See where you <em>fit.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede fx d4">The Compass is a written report on one swimmer and one list of schools. It scores their academics, their swimming, and everything else they do, then measures each score against the students that school actually enrolls. Every school on the list comes back with a plain read &mdash; strong fit, fits with a push, or long shot &mdash; and what would have to change to move up.</p>

      <div class="hero-actions fx d5">
        <a class="btn-gold" href="#get-the-compass">Get the Compass &mdash; $275</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="#how-it-works">How it works <span class="dn">&darr;</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-fine fx d5">One-time, per athlete. Includes every school on your list.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="scroll-cue">
    <span>SCROLL</span>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M6 9 L12 15 L18 9" stroke="#8FA0B3" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ==========================================================
     THE THREE INPUTS
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <h2>Three inputs. One score.</h2>
      <p>Each one plays a different role in your fit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="three">
      <div class="tcard reveal">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M20 9 L34 15 L20 21 L6 15 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/>
            <path d="M11 18 L11 26 C11 28 15 30 20 30 C25 30 29 28 29 26 L29 18" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M34 15 L34 24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Academics</h3>
        <p>Grades, test scores, and how hard the classes were.</p>
        <span class="role">Opens the door</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tcard reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <circle cx="26" cy="12" r="3.4" fill="#0F2A4A"/>
            <path d="M8 22 L17 18 L23 22 L30 19" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M6 28 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M6 33 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Athletics</h3>
        <p>How fast they swim, how fast they are getting, and across how many strokes.</p>
        <span class="role">Pushes you through</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tcard reveal" style="transition-delay:.2s">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M20 7 L23.6 15.2 L32.5 16 L25.8 21.9 L27.8 30.6 L20 26 L12.2 30.6 L14.2 21.9 L7.5 16 L16.4 15.2 Z" fill="#C9A13B" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Activities</h3>
        <p>Leadership, work, service, and everything else they do.</p>
        <span class="role role-soft">Adds support</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-divider reveal"><span>How academics &amp; athletics interact</span></div>

    <div class="gate-panel reveal">
      <h3 class="gate-headline">Grades open the door.<br>Speed gets you through.</h3>
      <div class="gate">
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-ic">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <rect x="9" y="5" width="14" height="22" rx="1.5" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8"/>
              <circle cx="19" cy="16" r="1.6" fill="#C9A13B"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Good grades</h3>
          <p>Open the door on their own.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-ic">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <path d="M16 25 L16 9" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <path d="M9 15 L16 8 L23 15" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Fast swimming</h3>
          <p>Gets a coach to open it for them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="gate-rule">Together, they decide whether the door opens.<br>Activities strengthens the case once it does.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     THE READ — what comes back per school
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <h2>Every school reads differently.</h2>
      <p>The same swimmer can land in three different bands across one list.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fits">
      <div class="fit g reveal">
        <span class="band-tag">Band A</span>
        <div class="fit-ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M6 14.5 L12 20 L22 8" stroke="#2E7D4F" stroke-width="2.4" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Strong fit</h3>
        <p>In range on academics alone. Swimming is a bonus.</p>
        <div class="fit-compare">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">You</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:80%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">School</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:60%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fit a reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">
        <span class="band-tag">Band B</span>
        <div class="fit-ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M14 7 L14 21 M7 14 L21 14" stroke="#8A6D16" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Fits with a push</h3>
        <p>A little below. A coach spending a spot can close the gap.</p>
        <div class="fit-compare">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">You</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">School</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:84%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fit r reveal" style="transition-delay:.2s">
        <span class="band-tag">Band C</span>
        <div class="fit-ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M8 24 L8 5 L21 8.5 L8 12" stroke="#A5502B" stroke-width="2.2" fill="none" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Long shot</h3>
        <p>Well below. Only a standout swimmer earns one of the few spots.</p>
        <div class="fit-compare">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">You</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:74%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">School</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:95%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note reveal">A guide to plan with. A coach&rsquo;s preread makes the real call.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     CHAPTER BREAK — the methodology half begins
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="chapter" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chapter-inner reveal">
      <span class="chapter-num">Part Two</span>
      <h2>How it works.</h2>
      <p>What goes in, how it is benchmarked, what comes out, and what it does not mean. Keep scrolling &mdash; the whole method is below.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     THE LANDSCAPE — what other tools measure
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">The landscape</span>
      <h2>What the other tools measure &mdash; and what they leave out.</h2>
      <p>Most families arrive having already tried two or three of these. Each answers a real question. None of them answer the whole one.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="land-grid">
      <div class="land-card reveal">
        <span class="land-kind">Swim recruiting indexes</span>
        <h3>A score built from your times</h3>
        <p class="land-eg">SwimCloud&rsquo;s Power Index and similar</p>
        <p class="land-method"><b>Method, as published:</b> your four fastest events are scored against the times needed to qualify for the NCAA Division I championships, then weighted &mdash; the top two events count fully, the third about a quarter, the fourth barely at all.</p>
        <div class="land-split">
          <div class="ls yes"><span>Measures</span><p>Speed, on a national scale. Genuinely useful, and openly documented.</p></div>
          <div class="ls no"><span>Cannot see</span><p>A transcript. Two swimmers with the same index read identically whether one has a 4.0 or a 2.9.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="land-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.08s">
        <span class="land-kind">Academic Index calculators</span>
        <h3>The Ivy 60&ndash;240 number</h3>
        <p class="land-eg">Top Tier Admissions, Oriel, and others</p>
        <p class="land-method"><b>Method, as published:</b> reconstruct the Ivy League&rsquo;s Academic Index &mdash; an unweighted GPA converted to points, plus a converted SAT or ACT score, on a 60 to 240 scale.</p>
        <div class="land-split">
          <div class="ls yes"><span>Measures</span><p>The academic gate. This one is real &mdash; it is the first number a coach&rsquo;s preread runs.</p></div>
          <div class="ls no"><span>Cannot see</span><p>Athletics at all &mdash; which is the reason the Academic Index was invented in the first place.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="land-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.16s">
        <span class="land-kind">Chancing engines</span>
        <h3>A percentage chance of admission</h3>
        <p class="land-eg">CollegeVine and similar</p>
        <p class="land-method"><b>Method, as published:</b> roughly 75 factors run through a machine-learning model trained on self-reported acceptance results, covering 1,500-plus schools and returning a single percentage.</p>
        <div class="land-split">
          <div class="ls yes"><span>Measures</span><p>How a general applicant compares to a general applicant pool. Large sample, fast answer.</p></div>
          <div class="ls no"><span>Cannot see</span><p>Recruiting. A coach&rsquo;s support is the single largest factor in a recruited athlete&rsquo;s file, and it is not in the model.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="land-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.24s">
        <span class="land-kind">Swim fit finders</span>
        <h3>A ranked list of programs</h3>
        <p class="land-eg">University Swim Fit, RecruitAI, On The Board, and similar</p>
        <p class="land-method"><b>Method, as published:</b> schools are ranked or bucketed using times, academics, cost, and location. The inputs are listed; the weights, benchmarks, and thresholds generally are not.</p>
        <div class="land-split">
          <div class="ls yes"><span>Measures</span><p>Closest in intent to the Compass &mdash; both axes, one list.</p></div>
          <div class="ls no"><span>Cannot see</span><p>Nothing structurally. But if a method is not published, a family cannot judge whether to trust the ranking.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="land-us reveal">
      <span class="land-us-label">Where the Compass sits</span>
      <p>We run both axes &mdash; the academic gate and the athletic tier &mdash; against <em>one specific school&rsquo;s own enrolled class</em>, not a national bar. Then we say how confident we are. The method below is the part most of these services do not publish.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     WHAT GOES IN
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">What goes in</span>
      <h2>Not a GPA + SAT calculator.</h2>
      <p>Six categories of information shape every assessment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="category-row reveal">
      <div class="category-chip">
        <div class="ic-sm"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 8 L27 12 L16 16 L5 12 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/><path d="M9 14.4 L9 19.5 C9 21 12 22.5 16 22.5 C20 22.5 23 21 23 19.5 L23 14.4" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/></svg></div>
        <span>Academic profile</span>
      </div>
      <div class="category-chip">
        <div class="ic-sm"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M7 24 L7 13 L16 7 L25 13 L25 24 Z" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none" stroke-linejoin="round"/><line x1="13" y1="24" x2="13" y2="18" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4"/><line x1="19" y1="24" x2="19" y2="18" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg></div>
        <span>High-school context</span>
      </div>
      <div class="category-chip">
        <div class="ic-sm"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="22" cy="9" r="2.6" fill="#0F2A4A"/><path d="M6 18 L13 15 L18 18 L24 15.5" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M5 22 q3 -3 6 0 q3 3 6 0 q3 -3 6 0 q3 3 6 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/></svg></div>
        <span>Athletics</span>
      </div>
      <div class="category-chip">
        <div class="ic-sm"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 6 L18.9 12.6 L26 13.3 L20.6 17.9 L22.2 24.8 L16 21 L9.8 24.8 L11.4 17.9 L6 13.3 L13.1 12.6 Z" fill="#C9A13B" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div>
        <span>Extracurricular profile</span>
      </div>
      <div class="category-chip">
        <div class="ic-sm"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="10" y1="6" x2="10" y2="26" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M10 7 L23 10.5 L10 14 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <span>University-specific data</span>
      </div>
      <div class="category-chip">
        <div class="ic-sm"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="9" cy="16" r="2" fill="#C9A13B"/><circle cx="16" cy="16" r="2" fill="#C9A13B"/><circle cx="23" cy="16" r="2" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <span>Other characteristics</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pipeline reveal">
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="pipeline-num"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="16" cy="11" r="4.2" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M7 26 C7 20 11 17 16 17 C21 17 25 20 25 26" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div>
        <h4>Inputs</h4>
        <p>Grades, times, activities</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="pipeline-num"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="7" y="7" width="18" height="4.5" rx="1.2" fill="#C9A13B"/><rect x="7" y="13.8" width="18" height="4.5" rx="1.2" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.4"/><rect x="7" y="20.6" width="18" height="4.5" rx="1.2" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg></div>
        <h4>Indices</h4>
        <p>Three independent scores</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="pipeline-num"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="5" y="13" width="22" height="6" rx="1.3" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6"/><line x1="10" y1="13" x2="10" y2="19" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="16" y2="19" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4"/><line x1="22" y1="13" x2="22" y2="19" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg></div>
        <h4>Standardize</h4>
        <p>One common scale</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="pipeline-num"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="10" y1="6" x2="10" y2="27" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M10 7 L23 10.5 L10 14 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <h4>Benchmark</h4>
        <p>Each school&rsquo;s own data</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="pipeline-num"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="6" y="18" width="4.5" height="9" rx="1" fill="#C9A13B"/><rect x="13.8" y="10" width="4.5" height="17" rx="1" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.4"/><rect x="21.5" y="14.5" width="4.5" height="12.5" rx="1" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <h4>Compare</h4>
        <p>Statistical comparison</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="pipeline-num"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="16" y1="6" x2="16" y2="15" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="16" y1="15" x2="9" y2="26" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="16" y1="15" x2="23" y2="26" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="9" cy="26" r="2.4" fill="#C9A13B"/><circle cx="23" cy="26" r="2.4" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <h4>Two outputs</h4>
        <p>Two distinct results</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     THE THREE INDICES
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Indices</span>
      <h2>Three independent indices, not one blended guess.</h2>
      <p>Academics, athletics, and profile are scored separately &mdash; then combined.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="three-idx reveal">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M20 9 L34 15 L20 21 L6 15 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/>
            <path d="M11 18 L11 26 C11 28 15 30 20 30 C25 30 29 28 29 26 L29 18" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M34 15 L34 24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Academics</h3>
        <p>Grades and test scores, turned into the number a coach&rsquo;s preread actually runs.</p>
        <div class="gauge"><span style="width:82%"></span></div>
        <div class="gauge-cap">8.2 / 10</div>
        <span class="role">Opens the door</span>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="tag">GPA</span><span class="tag">Test scores</span><span class="tag">Course rigor</span><span class="tag">Class rank</span><span class="tag">School context</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-note">A weak input redistributes weight rather than punishing the student for it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <circle cx="26" cy="12" r="3.4" fill="#0F2A4A"/>
            <path d="M8 22 L17 18 L23 22 L30 19" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M6 28 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M6 33 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0 q4 -4 8 0 q4 4 8 0" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Athletics</h3>
        <p>Their times against real college swimmers &mdash; plus the direction they are trending.</p>
        <div class="gauge"><span style="width:74%"></span></div>
        <div class="gauge-cap">7.4 / 10</div>
        <span class="role">Pushes you through</span>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="tag">Competitive times</span><span class="tag">Multi-year trend</span><span class="tag">Stroke range</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-note">Versatility is measured across strokes, not event count &mdash; four freestyle times is one stroke.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M20 7 L23.6 15.2 L32.5 16 L25.8 21.9 L27.8 30.6 L20 26 L12.2 30.6 L14.2 21.9 L7.5 16 L16.4 15.2 Z" fill="#C9A13B" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Activities</h3>
        <p>Rated on what an activity actually took, not which category it falls into.</p>
        <div class="gauge"><span style="width:66%"></span></div>
        <div class="gauge-cap">6.6 / 10</div>
        <span class="role role-soft">Adds support</span>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="tag">Leadership</span><span class="tag">Selectivity</span><span class="tag">Impact</span><span class="tag">Initiative</span><span class="tag">Years in</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-note">Fifteen shallow clubs score below one four-year commitment. Titles without time behind them are discounted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="combine reveal">
      <span class="combine-label">How they combine</span>
      <div class="equation-row">
        <span class="eq-chip">Academic Index</span>
        <span class="eq-op">+</span>
        <span class="eq-chip">Athletic Index</span>
        <span class="eq-op">=</span>
        <span class="eq-chip core">Core Score</span>
      </div>
      <div class="equation-row" style="margin-top:12px">
        <span class="eq-chip core">Core Score</span>
        <span class="eq-op">+</span>
        <span class="eq-chip adjust">Profile Index <i>(bounded adjustment)</i></span>
        <span class="eq-op">=</span>
        <span class="eq-chip final">Student-Athlete Score</span>
      </div>
      <p class="equation-caption">Profile strengthens a strong record. It can&rsquo;t sink it &mdash; and it can&rsquo;t replace it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     STANDARDIZE + BENCHMARK
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Standardize &rarr; Benchmark</span>
      <h2>Every number on the same scale. Measured against the right target.</h2>
      <p>Raw stats aren&rsquo;t comparable on their own &mdash; so we convert, then compare against each school&rsquo;s real data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid reveal">
      <div class="method-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="6" y="16" width="28" height="8" rx="1.5" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6"/><line x1="13" y1="16" x2="13" y2="24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="20" y1="16" x2="20" y2="24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="27" y1="16" x2="27" y2="24" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Standardization</h3>
        <p>A GPA, a test score, and a swim time don&rsquo;t compare directly. Every input is converted onto one common scale before anything is combined.</p>
        <div class="method-example">3.95 GPA &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; 1480 SAT &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; 52.10 free &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; one scale</div>
      </div>
      <div class="method-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="13" y1="7" x2="13" y2="33" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M13 8 L29 13 L13 18 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <h3>University benchmark</h3>
        <p>A school&rsquo;s target isn&rsquo;t one cutoff. We rebuild that school&rsquo;s own enrolled class as a distribution from its published data, and compare against that &mdash; not a universal bar.</p>
        <div class="method-example">Public admissions data &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; most recent class &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; updated annually</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="distribution-panel reveal">
      <div class="dist-label">A school&rsquo;s enrolled-class range</div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 600 170" width="100%" height="170" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img" aria-label="A bell curve showing a school's enrolled-class range, with a sample profile plotted on the upper half">
        <defs>
          <clipPath id="rangeClip"><rect x="180" y="0" width="240" height="170"/></clipPath>
        </defs>
        <path d="M20,150 C120,150 165,18 300,18 C435,18 480,150 580,150 L20,150 Z" fill="#C9A13B" opacity="0.16" clip-path="url(#rangeClip)"/>
        <path d="M20,150 C120,150 165,18 300,18 C435,18 480,150 580,150" fill="none" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <line x1="20" y1="150" x2="580" y2="150" stroke="#DED9CC" stroke-width="1"/>
        <line x1="375" y1="150" x2="375" y2="52" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
        <circle cx="375" cy="52" r="5.5" fill="#C9A13B" stroke="#0F2A4A" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      </svg>
      <div class="dist-caps">
        <span>Less competitive</span>
        <span class="dist-legend"><i></i> Sample profile</span>
        <span>More competitive</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pull-quote reveal">A profile isn&rsquo;t good or bad. Its competitiveness depends on the university it&rsquo;s measured against.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     OUTPUT 1 — STATISTICAL COMPARISON
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Output 1 &middot; Statistical comparison</span>
      <h2>A statistical comparison, not a lookup table.</h2>
      <p>The same swimmer, checked against three different university benchmarks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ex-athlete reveal">
      <span class="ex-label">Sample athlete</span>
      <div class="ex-stats">
        <div class="ex-stat"><b>8.2</b><span>Academics</span></div>
        <div class="ex-stat"><b>7.4</b><span>Athletics</span></div>
        <div class="ex-stat"><b>6.6</b><span>Activities</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cmp-list reveal">
      <div class="cmp">
        <div class="cmp-school">Selective school</div>
        <div class="cmp-bars">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">Sample athlete</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">This school</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:66%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
        <span class="chip s">Above range</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp">
        <div class="cmp-school">Highly selective school</div>
        <div class="cmp-bars">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">Sample athlete</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">This school</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:84%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
        <span class="chip s">Within range</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp">
        <div class="cmp-school">Most selective school</div>
        <div class="cmp-bars">
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">Sample athlete</span><div class="mbar"><i class="you" style="width:76%"></i></div></div>
          <div class="mini"><span class="mk">This school</span><div class="mbar"><i class="them" style="width:93%"></i></div></div>
        </div>
        <span class="chip s">Below range</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cmp-caption reveal">Nothing about the athlete changed &mdash; only the benchmark did. That&rsquo;s why the read is school-specific, not universal.</p>

    <div class="confidence-wrap reveal">
      <div class="confidence-bar">
        <div class="confidence-zone" style="left:40%;width:20%"></div>
        <div class="confidence-marker" style="left:50%"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="confidence-cap"><span>Below range</span><span>Within range</span><span>Above range</span></div>
      <p class="equation-caption">Reported as a range, not a percentage. A single number like &ldquo;87%&rdquo; hides how much the estimate could move; a range shows it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     OUTPUT 2 — THE PREREAD READ
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s navy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Output 2 &middot; Holistic Compass assessment</span>
      <h2>Grades open the door. Speed gets you through.</h2>
      <p>An academic gate and an athletic tier, read the way a selective coach&rsquo;s preread would &mdash; not a reproduction of any school&rsquo;s process.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ladder reveal">
      <div class="rung g"><span class="rung-k">Strong grades</span><span class="rung-v">In range on their own. Swimming is a bonus.</span></div>
      <div class="rung a"><span class="rung-k">Okay grades</span><span class="rung-v">Being fast helps a coach pick them.</span></div>
      <div class="rung r"><span class="rung-k">Lower grades</span><span class="rung-v">They&rsquo;d need to be a top swimmer.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="band-wrap reveal">
      <div class="band-scale"></div>
      <div class="band-caps"><span>Long shot</span><span>Fits with a push</span><span>Strong fit</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="gate-footnote reveal">Activities layers on top of this baseline. It doesn&rsquo;t replace it &mdash; and a thin activities record cannot pull a strong swimmer down more than a few points.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==========================================================
     LIMITATIONS
     ========================================================== -->
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head reveal">
      <span class="s-num">Limitations</span>
      <h2>What the Compass does not mean.</h2>
      <p>Worth saying plainly, because most tools in this category don&rsquo;t.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="limit-grid reveal">
      <div class="limit-card">
        <div class="limit-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="14" cy="14" r="10" stroke="#A5502B" stroke-width="1.6"/><line x1="7.5" y1="20.5" x2="20.5" y2="7.5" stroke="#A5502B" stroke-width="1.6"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Not a prediction</h3>
        <p>Admissions are holistic and dynamic &mdash; no index can fully capture them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="limit-card">
        <div class="limit-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="14" cy="14" r="10" stroke="#A5502B" stroke-width="1.6"/><line x1="7.5" y1="20.5" x2="20.5" y2="7.5" stroke="#A5502B" stroke-width="1.6"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Not a guarantee</h3>
        <p>We don&rsquo;t guarantee admission, offers, roster spots, or scholarships.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="limit-card">
        <div class="limit-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="14" cy="14" r="9" stroke="#C9A13B" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M14 7.5 L15.8 14 L14 20.5 L12.2 14 Z" fill="#C9A13B"/></svg></div>
        <h3>A read on fit, not an outcome</h3>
        <p>Built to show competitiveness and fit &mdash; not whether a student will be admitted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

